"How fast do the vocal folds open and close? Much faster than you can see. In a man's voice, they do it about 125 times every second. In a woman's voice, it is about 210 times, and in a child's voice, more than 300. Faster means a higher sound. To sing a high note, tiny muscles stretch your vocal folds longer and tighter, like a rubber band pulled tight. Children have high voices because their vocal folds are short. As you grow, they get longer, and your voice gets lower.": "fa6b95714058",
